"""
win_quantum_information.py

WIN Paradigm — Quantum Information Properties of the 8×8 Torus

The WIN substrate is an 8×8 torus lattice with 14 modes at λ = 4.
This script computes its real quantum information properties:

  1. Entanglement entropy of each mode
  2. Entanglement spectrum
  3. Out-of-time-order correlator (OTOC)
  4. Scrambling time
  5. Page curve of the 14-mode subspace
  6. Spectral form factor

These are standard quantum information calculations. They are derived
from the torus Laplacian. No invented formulas.

